Late last night, our network sensors flagged unusual traffic leaving 
the server at 192.168.1.100. An intruder breached our defenses and 
exfiltrated critical data, but their method is unclear. We’ve captured 
the traffic in a PCAP file—your job is to figure out how they did it and 
recover what they stole. The flag is hidden in the evidence, waiting to 
be uncovered.

File: breach.pcapng


Hint:

The echoes of the breach aren’t in the usual places—look beyond the payload to the signals themselves.